{{Quote|This here contains a fragment of my people's history. Our culture. Art. Music. Memories.''"<br />"''A Separatist archive. Fascinating.''"<br />"''Not Separatist. Serennian. We did exist before the war, you know.''"<br />"''I&hellip;never thought of it like that.|Serennian [[Romar Adell]] and former [[clone trooper]] [[Tech]]|<ref name="Ruins of War">{{TBB|Ruins of War}}</ref>}}
'''Serennians''' were a cultural group of [[human]]s native to the [[planet]] [[Serenno]]. Serennian [[Noble|nobility]] could be identified by the wearing of a [[Serennian cloak]], such as the ones worn by [[Count]] [[Dooku]] and [[Duke]] [[Solha]] and his siblings, a symbol of their status. Serennian custom permitted a condemned [[prisoner]] one last request. While Solha was proud of Serenno's membership within the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], heralding the world as part of a free [[star system]],<ref name="Thrawn: Alliances" /> Dooku exploited his own people during the [[Clone Wars]], creating internal strife on his homeworld.<ref name="Ruins of War" /> All the same, Serenno remained a major Separatist planet throughout the [[Clone Wars]], in large part because of its status as Dooku's birthplace<ref name="RiseFall">''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''</ref> and base-of-operations. Some Serennians, such as [[Romar Adell]], fled into Serenno's forests to escape [[Occupation of Serenno|Imperial occupation]].<ref name="Comprehensive SWE">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref>

